    'If the constraint is distinct from the pluralist reading, it must be because the Magisterial authority claim is structurally essential—not just a rhetorical wrapper. If the policies are separable from authority, then the ''constraint'' is really the shared policy cluster, and the readings are alternative legitimations of it. This is a conceptual omega about whether we have one constraint with multiple readings or multiple constraints with overlapping outputs.',
    confidence_without_resolution(low)
).

narrative_ontology:omega_variable(reading_distinctness_from_pluralist_pragmatic, conceptual, 'Whether the Magisterial reading''s distinctness depends on its authority claim or only on its policy outputs.').

