    suppression_internalization_tech_workers,
    'Is the measured suppression (0.35) structural (institutional exclusion of non-Catholic voices, policy restrictions on code) or partly internalized (tech workers with secular worldviews who have internalized the constraint through ESG training, ethical AI certification, or career incentives)? After the constraint is removed, does suppression persist?',
    'Post-exit analysis: survey technologists who have left regulated environments or faith-aligned institutions; assess whether constraint internalization persists. Track whether workers with secular commitments who adopt the constraint do so because they believe in it or because institutional pressure makes refusal costly.',
    'If suppression is largely structural, the constraint''s power depends on institutional enforcement—it decays if enforcement relaxes. If suppression is partly internalized, workers carry the constraint''s discipline with them even after exit; reclassification would show higher effective suppression than the measured 0.35. This affects the long-term stability prediction.',
    confidence_without_resolution(medium)
).

narrative_ontology:omega_variable(suppression_internalization_tech_workers, empirical, 'Extent to which suppression is structural or internalized in technologists'' self-discipline.').


